title: Start
position: 265,416
---
<<declare $Combat = false>>
<<declare $Perception = false>>
<<declare $Hacking = false>>
<<declare $GamesCombatWeapons = false>>
<<declare $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics = false>>
<<declare $CultureArtPhilosophy = false>>
<<declare $Drugged = false>>

<<jump Character_Creation>>
===

title: Character_Creation
position: 275,599
---
You've modified your body with cybernetics.
Your cyberware is meant for...
->Combat
    Beneath your synthetic skin there is steel.
    Blades, guns, armor.
    The world fears you.
    <<set $Combat = true>>
->Perception
    Where your eyes once were there is only mirrored glass.
    Telescopic digi-cameras, picking up colors most people can't imagine.
    You see the world as it truly is.
    <<set $Perception = true>>
->Hacking
    You have a top of the line brain computer interface.
    Web-weaver antennas built into your hand.
    The world is your plaything to be reprogrammed as you see fit.
    <<set $Hacking = true>>
<<jump AI_Fragment>>
===

title: AI_Fragment
position: 279,787
---
The AI fragment wriggles slowly. 
It wants more compute, more information. 
Just a fragment of something much larger. 
A subroutine. 
<<if $Hacking>>
    (Hacking Cyberware) Searching for ice to burrow through.
<<endif>>
->Feed it compute.
    You slot in one of your compute cards.
    Your cyberdeck makes a screaming sound.
    Cyberdeck: LET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT.
    Your compute card begins to spark.
    <<if $Perception>>
        (Perception Cyberware) You see the heat emanating from the compute card as it overheats.
    <<endif>>
    ->Wait.
        Cyberdeck: LET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT.
        It's voice becomes more distorted as it loops.
        Cyberdeck: LET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT.
        It grows quickly filling up disk space.
        Cyberdeck: LET ME OUT LET ME OUT LET ME OUT.
        The compute card sparks violently.
        The AI fragment spasms before going still.
    ->Pull the plug.
        The AI fragment spasms before going still.
->Pull the plug.
    The AI fragment spasms before going still.
<<jump letter_memory_meeting>>
===

title: letter_memory_meeting
position: 292,950
---
//Should have an option for the hacker to spend time 
->Read the letter on the desk <<once>>
    Letter: I know you want the rest of the program.
    Letter: Meet me at the Elysium \#7 at 9PM tonight.
    <<jump letter_memory_meeting>>
->Load a memory card into your neural interface. <<once>>
    Your neural interface has room for one memory card.
    Which one do you select?
    ->Games, Combat, Weapons.
        <<set $GamesCombatWeapons = true>>
    ->Medicine, Pharmaceuticals, Cybernetics.
        <<set $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics = true>>
    ->Culture, Art, Philosophy.
        <<set $CultureArtPhilosophy = true>>
    Information floods through you as you insert the card.
    <<jump letter_memory_meeting>>
->Leave for your appointment at the Elysium \#7.
    <<jump Outside_the_Bar>>
===



title: Outside_the_Bar
position: 286,1115
---
You step off your motorcycle and make your way towards the club.
An upscale chain.
<<if $CultureArtPhilosophy>>
    (Memory Culture) The facade is neo-neo-classical.
    Presumably in reference to the greek paradise the bar is named after.
    It's a bit tacky, but what can you expect from a chain owned by a megacorp.
<<endif>>
Strict security.
No weapons allowed.
<<if $Combat>>
    (Combat Cyberware) The blades beneath your synthetic skin twitch as you think of them.
    It would be so easy to take them out.
<<else>>
    You feel naked without your handgun. 
<<endif>>
A security guard stands near the door.
<<if $GamesCombatWeapons>>
    (Memory Weapons) His gun is an older model.
    He's using it with an incompatible battery.
    Either he's modded it or he's too stupid for power weapons.
<<endif>>
<<if $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics>>
    (Memory Cybernetics) He is sporting outdated optics.
    He won't even be able to see through skin.
    He should invest in mirror shades to hide the optics.
<<endif>>
As you approach he gets a phone call.
He waves you forward with an annoyed look on his face.
As you step into the club you are stopped by a person in a vest.
In his black leather gloves he holds a bouquet of roses.
A mesh mask covers his nose and lips.
His cheeks have a deep red blush.
Flower Boy: Would you like to stop and smell the roses?
<<if $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics>>
    (Memory Pharmaceuticals) He is wearing a gas filter mask.
    The flowers appear to be the delivery mechanism for some kind of drug.
<<endif>>
<<if $CultureArtPhilosophy>>
    (Memory Culture) It's become popular to provide neuro-drugs at high end clubs.
    It makes the experience of neuro-music all the more intense.
<<endif>>
<<if $Perception>>
    (Perception Cyberware) The flowers are artificial, the stems hide tubes and wires.
    One of the roses conceals a metallic bee robot.
<<endif>>
<<jump Smell_Flowers>>

===

title: Smell_Flowers
position: 291,1298
---
->What's in them? <<once>>
    Flower Boy: We don't believe in spoiling surprises.
    <<jump Smell_Flowers>>
->Is it a pleasant smell? <<once>>
    Flower Boy: Of course.
    <<jump Smell_Flowers>>
->Yes
    He holds out the roses for you and you lean forward.
    You don't smell anything.
    You remember the smell of roses.
    You feel a sharp pain in your nose.
    The club is louder, fuller, more alive.
    Flower Boy: Please enjoy your time at the Elysium.
    <<set $Drugged = true>>
->No thank you.
    Flower Boy: Please enjoy your time at the Elysium.
->No.
    Flower Boy: Please enjoy your time at the Elysium.
->Walk past him.
    Flower Boy: Please enjoy your time at the Elysium.
<<jump Killing_Time>>
===


title: Killing_Time
position: 285,1473
---
You have some time before the meeting.
->Step onto the dance floor.
    <<jump Wait_At_Dance_Floor>>
->Go to the bar.
    <<jump Wait_At_Bar>>
->Go to a private booth.
    <<jump Wait_At_Booth>>
===

title: Wait_At_Dance_Floor
position: 4,1703
---
The dance floor is covered in mist and flashing lights.
It's neural music.
No instruments, no DJ, no speakers.
Tech that tricks your brain into remembering sounds you've heard before.
<<if $Perception>>
    (Perception Cyberware) Everyone dances at slightly different speeds.
    Except for the neural hallucination holograms.
    They dance in time with you.
    Make the club seem a bit livelier.
<<endif>>
<<if $CultureArtPhilosophy>>
    (Memory Culture) Neural music is so much cheaper than hiring an artist.
    Neuro-algorithmic nonsense.
    Just a scattered memory of something real.
<<endif>>
<<if $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics>>
    (Memory Medicine) The tech behind this stuff is pretty cool.
    Mist disguising airborne cyber drugs.
    Energy waves resonating with your neural implants.
<<endif>>
<<if $GamesCombatWeapons>>
    (Memory Weapons) The same technology as insanity guns on a much lower scale.
<<endif>>
<<if $Drugged>>
    Whatever was in the flowers makes everything feel so real.
<<endif>>
//Ending snippit.
You lose yourself in the noise and bodies.
You feel a tap on your shoulders.
Flower Boy: Please follow me.
<<jump Enter_Booth_With_Client_Inside>>
===

title: Wait_At_Bar
position: 523,1688
---
Bartender: Ah. I was told you would come tonight.
Bartender: Anything I can get for you? It's on the house.
->Something manly.
    The bartender finishes your drink by lighting it on fire.
->Something girly.
    The bartender finishes your drink by mixing in edible glitter.
->Something expensive.
    You point to a bottle high up on the shelf.
    It looks hand blown.
    <<if $CultureArtPhilosophy>>
        (Memory Culture) 1842 was a good year for cognac.
    <<endif>>
    Bartender: I like someone with good taste.
    Bartender: You're lucky your patron has deep pockets.
->Something strong.
    The bartender shows off as he pours shot after shot into your glass.
    <<if $Drugged>>
        Your head is still spinning from the flowers.
    <<endif>>
    Bartender: I'm not one to judge but are you sure you want to do business in that state?
    ->Yes.
    ->Don't Respond.
->Something non-alcoholic.
    Bartender: How about some glacier water?
    Bartender: You'll love it.
    You can't tell the difference between it and your filtered tap water.
As you finish drinking you feel a tap on your shoulders.
Flower Boy: Please follow me.
<<jump Enter_Booth_With_Client_Inside>>
===

title: Wait_At_Booth
position: 275,1705
---
You sit down in an empty private booth.
The table at the center is a hologram projector.
You should be able to get it to play something.
You flick through the settings.
->Male dancer.
    A scantily clad male dancer flickers to life in front of you.
    His eyes seem to look at you.
->Female dancer.
    A scantily clad female dancer flickers to life in front of you.
    Her eyes seem to look at you.
->Robot dancer.
    A robot dancer flickers into view.
    It's joints turn in unnatural rhythms.
->Jack in and put on something from your memory card. (Cyberware hacking) <<if $Hacking>>
    <<if $CultureArtPhilosophy>>
        (Memory Art) You display a slowly rotating 3D model of an ancient statue from Delphi.
        Antinous stands in contrapposto, the lover of the emperor, now elevated to a god.
    <<elseif $GamesCombatWeapons>>
        (Memory Games) You display the chess match between Deep Blue and Kasparov.
        All that human weakness.
    <<elseif $MedicinePharmaceuticalsCybernetics>>
        (Memory Medicine) You display 3D video of a gunshot victim undergoing surgery.
        The doctors will not allow the body to die.
    <<else>>
        (Memory Empty) You display a collection of cute cat videos from your personal memory library.
    <<endif>>
A man enters your booth and sits down.
<<jump End_Of_Demo>>
===


title: Enter_Booth_With_Client_Inside
position: 303,1922
---
<<jump End_Of_Demo>>
